      R. Q. 1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَضْفَضَ</span></b>  <i>He made</i> a garment, and a
coat of mail, <i>wide,</i> or <i>ample.</i> (TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  [Also,
probably, <i>It</i> (a garment, and a <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دِرْع</span> and (assumed tropical:)  the
means of subsistence,) <i>was,</i> or <i>became, wide,</i> or
<i>ample:</i> see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَضْفَضَةٌ</span>, below.]

